  },
  "body": "This clarifies an ambiguity with the case-sensitivity of attribute selectors using IDs and classes in quirks mode. While ID and class selectors such as `.foo` are case-insensitive in quirks mode, this is not the case with attribute selectors using the `id` and `class` attributes such as `[class=\"foo\"]`.\r\n\r\nThe previous wording, preceded by a paragraph mentioning attribute selectors, made this difference unclear as it referred only to \"IDs and classes\" rather than the specific selector types.",
